  "behavior": [
    "Version 1 keyframes keep their serialization and column order. Version 2 deltas are rejected by the original reader.",
    "Every delta own-row read checks a domain-separated ordered digest of table-name lengths/names, canonical row lengths/bytes, final count and byte total.",
    "The folded chain checks its actual base totals, sequence continuity, exact removals, duplicate additions, recomputed charges, final fingerprints and totals.",
    "Persisted metadata validation and the seal planner use the same base+charged-changes <=2*max(current,1) predicate for row counts and row bytes.",
    "Every delta charges at least one row and one byte, including empty seals. Oversized row/byte changes or tombstone bursts produce a full keyframe.",
    "Archive validation verifies all deltas, including those superseded by a later keyframe; real reopen rejects a substituted superseded delta row.",
    "The five-event cadence, replay limits, row/byte/record caps, schema version36 and immutable history remain unchanged."
  ],
